    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16639" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-carnĭfĭco</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a., <i>to cut</i> or <i>tear any one to
				pieces</i> (a rare word). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
					D. 3, 33 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
			24</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to torment</i>, <i>torture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 4, 6, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">excarnificatus animus, Sen. de Ira, 3, 4:
					comitem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 5, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">14, 9, 6</span></i>.</div>
